For consistency, we always use `??` instead of `||` for default fallbacks as `||` could lead to bugs in certain cases.

```suggestion
  const subGraphTitleTopMargin = getConfig().flowchart?.subGraphTitleMargin?.top ?? 0;
  const subGraphTitleBottomMargin = getConfig().flowchart?.subGraphTitleMargin?.bottom ?? 0;
```

Can you also remove the duplicate call to getConfig()?

```suggestion
  const { flowchart } = getConfig();
  const subGraphTitleTopMargin = flowchart?.subGraphTitleMargin?.top ?? 0;
  const subGraphTitleBottomMargin = flowchart?.subGraphTitleMargin?.bottom ?? 0;
```

Or even better, make config a parameter to the function, the config is already available from your callsites, so we can pass it in here, eliminating the call altogether.
